#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186135091 :tutorial/content "Remember that if $X$ is a binomial random variable in which there are $n$ experiments and $p$ is the probability of success on each experiment, then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x) = \\binom{n}{x} p^x (1-p)^{n-x}.\n$$\n\nIt can be shown that the expected value, variance, and standard deviation of a binomial random variable $X$ can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{E}[X] & =np \\\\ \\text{Var}[X] & =np(1-p) \\\\ \\text{SD}[X] & =\\sqrt{np(1-p)}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "872af947-d3c7-525f-8bb9-21d55de36921" :tutorial/math-academy-id 4452 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}]}
